      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, we first need to calculate the number of days from November 23 to December 23. We will do this by counting the days in each month, noting that November has 30 days and December has 31 days.\n\nThe number of days from November 23 to December 23 is:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ days (November)} + 23 \\text{ days (December)} = 53 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine what day of the week December 23 falls on. We know that November 23 is a Thursday. To find out what day of the week November 24 is, we add 1 day (since November 24 is the next day after November 23), which brings us to a Friday. We continue this process for each day, adding the number of days in each month until we reach December 23.\n\nWe can use the formula for finding the day of the week for a given date:\n\\[ \\text{Day of the week} = (\\text{Day of the month} + \\text{Number of days passed} + \\text{Start day}) \\mod 7 \\]\n\nHere, the start day is Thursday, the day of the month is 23, and the number of days passed from November 23 to December 23 is 53 days.\n\nLet's perform the calculation step by step:\n\\[ \\text{Day of the week} = (23 + 53 + 4) \\mod 7 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Day of the week} = (76 + 4) \\mod 7 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Day of the week} = 80 \\mod 7 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Day of the week} = 2 \\mod 7 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Day of the week} = 2 \\]\n\nSo, December 23 is 2 days after Thursday, which is a Saturday.\n\nTherefore, the day of the week for December 23 is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).",
